From 4d4ebf8908dbfedaa85fa6a7887cdd76227acaa7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Delgado <328510259+thinkddr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 12:37:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(software): a fractional position lands on the nearest
 pixel, as in GL

The software painter took the ceiling of every position (scale.ToScreenCoordinate),
so anything at a fractional coordinate was drawn a pixel lower or further right
than the GL painter (roundToPixel) and a browser draw it. Captures and image tests
are what the window is compared against, so they drifted from both. Positions and
the clip origin now round; sizes still round up so nothing loses its last partial
pixel.

Measured against Chromium with Figtree at eight fractional tops, the text baseline
now matches on all of them (it missed three). The 15 goldens that change move text
or an edge by one pixel.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
